~ initialize_local_variables

=> start

~ start
...Dad, where are you?
...[do DialogueFuncs.play_sfx("sfx_door_open")]
Sarah: [wait=1]...Oh. Hello. 
Sarah: You seen my father?
Sarah: I heard him come in late last night. I'm a light sleeper. 
Sarah: [#sprite=happy][do DialogueFuncs.play_sfx("sfx_giggle")]I could even hear you snore.
Sarah: But then he left again... and didn't come back.
- Haven't seen him since yesterday, myself. 
	Sarah: Hmm. Wonder what he's up to. => drink
- Know where he went?
	Sarah: Uh, not really. => drink

~ drink
Sarah: He used to drink. A lot. But he hasn't in a while.
Sarah: Don't remember him being gone for a whole night since he stopped. 
Sarah: I'm starting to get worried. 
- I'm sure he's fine. => what
- I can help you look for him, if you want. => help
- The Goddess is looking out for him. Don't worry. [if Variables.get_var("religious_fervour") >=6] 
	Sarah: I'm sure She is. But it's a bit more complicated than that. => hope
- Isn't the Goddess supposed to take care of him? Him being a Gift-bearer and whatnot? [if Variables.get_var("religious_fervour") <= 5]
	Sarah: [#sprite=upset]That's not how it works. Gift-bearers don't get special treatment. => hope

~ what
Sarah: [#sprite=upset]How can you be sure? You just got here. 
Sarah: [#sprite=upset]You don't know the first thing about us. 
- I was just trying to comfort you. 
	Sarah: [#sprite=upset]I don't want comfort. I want to find him. => hope
- You're right. I've no idea if he's fine or not. 
	Sarah: Oh, this is bad. => hope
- I don't know. It's just a thing you say. 
	Sarah: [#sprite=upset]I hate it when adults just say things. => hope
- I'm the Goddess's chosen one. If I say he's fine, then he's fine. [if Variables.get_var("religious_fervour") >=6]
	Sarah: [#sprite=upset]Uh huh. That's definitely not how it works. => hope

~ help
Sarah: [#sprite=upset]Appreciate it, but how would you help, exactly?
Sarah: There isn't a nook or cranny in this village I'm not familiar with. 
Sarah: [#sprite=upset]You may think I'm some worthless little girl, but I'm not. 
- I don't think you're worthless. I'm just trying to help. 
	Sarah: [#sprite=upset]Well, you can't. Plus, I'm managing just fine. => hope
- Confident, are we? 
	Sarah: [#sprite=upset]Laugh all you want. 
	Sarah: [#sprite=upset]You don't know what it was like. => anyway3
- How so?
	Sarah: I make sure he doesn't drink anymore. 
	Sarah: He's had some serious problems with it in the past. => anyway1
	
~ hope
Sarah: ...
Sarah: Oh, I really hope he didn't go drinking. 
- He doesn't beat you, does he? => beat
- Why's he not supposed to drink?
	Sarah: He's had some serious problems with it in the past. => anyway1

~ beat
Sarah: [#sprite=upset]What? No! Of course not!
Sarah: [#sprite=upset]Why would you think that?
Sarah: He's the sweetest, most caring dad in the world. He loves me more than anything. 
Sarah: He'd never lay a hand on me. 
- Just asking. 
	Sarah: [#sprite=upset]Weird thing to ask. 
	- Not really. 
		Sarah: [#sprite=upset]Yes really. You won't find that kind of thing here. The Goddess is strictly against it. => children
	- Guess so. 
		Sarah: [#sprite=upset]You won't find that kind of thing here, you know. The Goddess is strictly against it. => children
- Lots of heavy drinkers are also violent. That's all. 
	Sarah: [#sprite=upset]Yeah, well, you won't find that kind of thing here. => children
- Got some bad experiences with it myself. Just wanted to make sure. 
	Sarah: Oh, I'm sorry to hear that. 
	Sarah: But no. Like I said, he would never. 
	Sarah: And anyway, you won't find that kind of thing here. The Goddess is strictly against it. => children

~ children
Sarah: She says children are pure and holy. We're the future, the ones who will inhabit Her new world, once She's done cleansing it of sinners and evil-doers. 
Sarah: Parents who beat their children are punished. Maybe even killed.
Sarah: But that's never happened here, cause no one ever does it. 
- Good to know. => anyway2
- Built yourselves a proper little utopia here, have you?
	Sarah: Not sure what you mean by utopia. But we didn't build anything. It's all the work of the Goddess. 
	Sarah: [#sprite=happy]She loves us and She takes care of us. We're all indebted to Her for life. => anyway2
	
~ anyway1
Sarah: He'd get so drunk sometimes he couldn't find his way home at night. Used to find him in some ditch in the morning, passed out. 
Sarah: ...Thought he was dead this one time. 
Sarah: ...
Sarah: He's been clean three months now. Not a single sip. 
Sarah: I've been watching him. 
- I'm sorry. 
	Sarah: It's fine. It's all in the past. 
	Sarah: It was the Goddess who told him to stop. If he drinks again, he's in trouble. => vengeful
- He's lucky to have you. 
	Sarah: Course he is. And there's more than this one reason for it. 
	Sarah: It was the Goddess who told him to stop, you know? So if he drinks again, he's in trouble. => vengeful 
- That's fucked. 
	Sarah: [#sprite=upset]Language. 
	Sarah: It's fine. It's all in the past, anyway. 
	Sarah: It was the Goddess who told him to stop, you know? So if he drinks again, he's in trouble. => vengeful
- Uhh... I'm really not sure what to say to that. 
	Sarah: Don't worry. You don't have to say anything. 
	Sarah: [#sprite=upset]Adults rarely know what to say.
	Sarah: It was the Goddess who told him to stop, you know? So if he drinks again, he's in trouble. => vengeful
- I don't need to know all that. 
	Sarah: [#sprite=upset]You're the one who asked. 
	Sarah: [#sprite=upset]Quite heartless, aren't you?[do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_2", "relationship", 0)] => micah2

