~ vengeful 
- The Goddess is vengeful, isn't She?
	Sarah: She can be. She can also be merciful and fair. 
	Sarah: She's whatever She needs to be. 
	Sarah: It's not for us to question Her. 
	- If you say so. 
		Sarah: [#sprite=upset]It's not so because I say so. It is so because She says so. => micah
	- You're wise for your age. [if Variables.get_var("religious_fervour") >= 6]
		Sarah: [#sprite=happy]Course I am. [do Variables.mod_var("religious_fervour", 1)] => micah
	- Guess you're right. 
		Sarah: [#sprite=happy]Course I am. => micah
	- Eh, not sure how I feel about that. 
		Sarah: You'll see the light, eventually. 
	- That's... not how it should work. [if Variables.get_var("religious_fervour") <= 5]
		Sarah: [#sprite=upset]Who are you to say? You should know your place. => micah
- What kind of trouble?
	Sarah: I don't know. It's not for me to say. 
	Sarah: But it sure won't be pretty. She very rarely gives orders directly to us, mortals, individually. 
	Sarah: She must have had Her reasons, and they must have been important. 
	Sarah: So I gotta be super careful and make sure my dad doesn't disobey Her. 
	Sarah: I love him and I'm sure he loves the Goddess, but he has his moments of weakness from time to time. 
	- I see. => micah
	- Weakness? 
		Sarah: I sometimes fear he's not as devoted to the Goddess as he should be. 
		Sarah: I've seen him nearly cry over the most unimportant things sometimes. Things outside of his control. Things the Goddess told us don't matter. I don't get it. 
		Sarah: Anyway, that's our business. => micah

~ micah
Micah: [wait=1.5][do DialogueFuncs.play_sfx("sfx_door_open")][#sprite=happy]Morning, Sarah. Fresh delivery for you, novice. Hahah. You already look like you own the place. [do DialogueFuncs.add_object_to_workbench("milk_carton_variant_02")][do DialogueFuncs.add_object_to_workbench("book_01")]
Sarah: Micah! Have you seen my father? He didn't come home last night.
Micah: Sure have. He's with the Elders. No idea why, though. He was with 'em late into the night. 
Micah: I tried to listen in but couldn't hear shit. 
Micah: [#sprite=upset]...Uh, sorry.
Micah: He just up and left at one point. He seemed angry.
Micah: He came back this morning. He's still there, now. I think.
Sarah: [#sprite=happy]Oh thank the Goddess. I was starting to get worried. 
Sarah: [#sprite=upset]Thought he started drinking again. I'll have a word with him tonight. 
Sarah: [#sprite=happy]Anyway, I'm ready. Shall we?
Micah: [#sprite=happy]Uh, sure. 
- Where are you two going?
	Micah: Uh, we can't tell you. [do Variables.set_var("knows_of_gift", true)]
	Sarah: [#sprite=happy]Sure we can. You can keep a secret, can't you?
	Sarah: My dad's birthday is coming up in a few days. Micah's helping me get him a surprise gift. 
	Sarah: [#sprite=happy]It's gonna be really cool. But I can't tell you what it is yet. I don't trust you quite enough.
	Sarah: [#sprite=happy]But since you're Gifted and all, you might help cleanse it right before we give it to him. Have the Goddess bless it through you!
	Sarah: [#sprite=happy]What do you say?
	- Sure thing. 
		Sarah: [#sprite=happy]Awesome. Thanks! [do Variables.set_char_var("NPC_2", "relationship", 3)]
		Sarah: [#sprite=happy]Anyway, see you later. 
		Sarah: If dad shows up tell him I'm with Micah, and that I'll be back before nightfall. And make him go sleep! 
		Sarah: [#sprite=upset]And if you mention the surprise, you're dead!
		Micah: [#sprite=happy]See you later, fake 'Keeper! [do DialogueFuncs.play_sfx("sfx_door_close")]
